      "title": "Bauhinia x goes TEDx",
      "abstract": "<p>The botanical (latin) name for the Hong Kong Bauhinia flower is\n&lt;em&gt;\n Bauhinia x blakeana\n&lt;/em&gt;\n, with the x denoting it is a hybrid between two species. In the hierarchy of TED talks, TEDx are independent TED-like events organised by volunteers such as universities agreeing to follow certain principles. Bauhinia x has finally met TEDx, with Scott\u2019s talk at TEDxEduHK just being posted online today.</p>",
